From the ankle to the upper thigh, there are five steps, and repeat each movement ten times:
1. Starting at the ankle, use both thumbs to push and press the calf muscle from bottom to top;
2. Use the palm to knead and rub the outer calf up to the knee;
3. Starting above the knee, use the heel of the palm to press the front thigh;
4. Use the thumb to press the inner thigh, from above the knee to the groin;
5. Finally, wrap the palm around the back of the thigh and push upward from the knee crease to the buttocks.
The key is to promote blood circulation and prevent blood clots.
